  <!-- ===== OVERLAYS (kept for future use) ===== -->

  <div class="overlay" id="overlay-phase-1" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog" aria-label="Resources for when you just left">
    <div class="overlay-backdrop"></div>
    <div class="overlay-panel">
      <button class="overlay-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
      <div class="overlay-content">
        <span class="overline">Phase 1: Immediate Aftermath</span>
        <h2>You're safe now. That matters.</h2>
        <p>The confusion you're feeling - the fog, the fear, the guilt tangled with relief - is your mind processing what you survived. It's not a flaw. It's a natural response.</p>
        <div class="carousel-row"><h3 class="carousel-label">Something gentle for your ears</h3><div class="carousel"><button class="carousel-arrow carousel-prev" aria-label="Scroll left">&lsaquo;</button><div class="carousel-track"><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Meditation</span><h4>Guided Meditation for Victims of Domestic Abuse</h4><p class="carousel-source">Fragrant Heart</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Meditation</span><h4>Grounding Meditation for Trauma</h4><p class="carousel-source">Insight Timer - Dr. Amelia Kelley</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Meditation</span><h4>I Am Safe: Healing from Terror/Trauma</h4><p class="carousel-source">Insight Timer</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Podcast</span><h4>4 Steps to Break a Trauma Bond</h4><p class="carousel-source">The Relationship Recovery Podcast - EP102</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Podcast</span><h4>Love and Abuse</h4><p class="carousel-source">Paul Colaianni</p></a></div><button class="carousel-arrow carousel-next" aria-label="Scroll right">&rsaquo;</button></div></div>
        <div class="carousel-row"><h3 class="carousel-label">Words that understand</h3><div class="carousel"><button class="carousel-arrow carousel-prev" aria-label="Scroll left">&lsaquo;</button><div class="carousel-track"><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Article</span><h4>Stages of Recovery After Trauma</h4><p class="carousel-source">DomesticShelters.org</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Article</span><h4>What Is Trauma Bonding?</h4><p class="carousel-source">DomesticShelters.org</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Guide</span><h4>I've Left and I Need Support</h4><p class="carousel-source">Women's Aid - The Survivor's Handbook</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Article</span><h4>5 Powerful Self-Care Tips for Abuse and Trauma Survivors</h4><p class="carousel-source">The Hotline</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Guide</span><h4>Create Your Personal Safety Plan</h4><p class="carousel-source">The Hotline</p></a></div><button class="carousel-arrow carousel-next" aria-label="Scroll right">&rsaquo;</button></div></div>
        <div class="carousel-row"><h3 class="carousel-label">Stories like yours</h3><div class="carousel"><button class="carousel-arrow carousel-prev" aria-label="Scroll left">&lsaquo;</button><div class="carousel-track"><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">TED Talk</span><h4>Why Domestic Violence Victims Don't Leave</h4><p class="carousel-source">Leslie Morgan Steiner</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">TEDx Talk</span><h4>I Left on a Tuesday</h4><p class="carousel-source">Chiara Lisowski</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">YouTube Channel</span><h4>Dr. Ramani Durvasula</h4><p class="carousel-source">YouTube</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">TEDx Talk</span><h4>Domestic Violence: What Everyone Needs to Know</h4><p class="carousel-source">Hannah Petrillo</p></a><a href="#" class="carousel-card"><span class="carousel-type">Exercise</span><h4>Trauma-Sensitive 5-4-3-2-1 Grounding Exercise</h4><p class="carousel-source">Insight Timer</p></a></div><button class="carousel-arrow carousel-next" aria-label="Scroll right">&rsaquo;</button></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="overlay" id="overlay-phase-2" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog" aria-label="Resources for when you feel stuck">
    <div class="overlay-backdrop"></div>
    <div class="overlay-panel">
      <button class="overlay-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
      <div class="overlay-content">
        <span class="overline">Phase 2: The Middle</span>
        <h2>Stuck doesn't mean broken.</h2>
        <p>You're safe, but the weight of everything is surfacing. Grief for the relationship, anger you couldn't express before, and the question "who am I without this?" are all part of this phase.</p>
        <div class="overlay-cards"><div class="overlay-card"><h4>Grief without closure</h4><p>You're mourning someone still alive, a relationship that held both love and violence. Society rarely validates this grief.</p></div><div class="overlay-card"><h4>Anger is arriving</h4><p>Anger was unsafe to express during the relationship. Feeling it now is healthy - even when it's frightening.</p></div><div class="overlay-card"><h4>Identity is rebuilding</h4><p>Your preferences, opinions, and sense of self were systematically eroded. Rediscovering them takes time and patience.</p></div></div>
        <div class="overlay-resources"><h3>What might help right now</h3><a href="#wellness" class="overlay-link" data-close-overlay>Trauma-informed yoga for body reconnection &rarr;</a><a href="#wellness" class="overlay-link" data-close-overlay>Mindfulness practices for self-exploration &rarr;</a><a href="#community" class="overlay-link" data-close-overlay>Daily check-ins with the community &rarr;</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="overlay" id="overlay-phase-3" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog" aria-label="Resources for rebuilding">
    <div class="overlay-backdrop"></div>
    <div class="overlay-panel">
      <button class="overlay-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
      <div class="overlay-content">
        <span class="overline">Phase 3: Rebuilding</span>
        <h2>You're becoming someone new.</h2>
        <p>Rebuilding trust, setting boundaries, navigating new relationships - this phase is simultaneously liberating and terrifying. Growth and pain coexist here, and that's okay.</p>
        <div class="overlay-cards"><div class="overlay-card"><h4>Boundaries are new</h4><p>You may swing between walls and no boundaries at all. Learning the middle ground is a practice, not a destination.</p></div><div class="overlay-card"><h4>Trust takes time</h4><p>Learning to distinguish healthy from unhealthy patterns - in others and in yourself - is part of earned secure attachment.</p></div><div class="overlay-card"><h4>Post-traumatic growth</h4><p>Deeper empathy, clarity about values, new life directions. Not universal, but possible - and it coexists with ongoing pain.</p></div></div>
        <div class="overlay-resources"><h3>What might help right now</h3><a href="#wellness" class="overlay-link" data-close-overlay>Wellness programs for ongoing healing &rarr;</a><a href="#community" class="overlay-link" data-close-overlay>Peer support and mentorship &rarr;</a><a href="#community" class="overlay-link" data-close-overlay>Weekly community events &rarr;</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="overlay" id="overlay-breathing" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog" aria-label="Guided breathing resources">
    <div class="overlay-backdrop"></div>
    <div class="overlay-panel">
      <button class="overlay-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
      <div class="overlay-content">
        <span class="overline">Learn to Breathe Better</span>
        <h2>Calm starts with a single breath.</h2>
        <p>When your body is stuck in fight-or-flight, breathing is the fastest way back to safety. These exercises are simple, short, and available anytime you need them.</p>
        <div class="breathing-exercise" role="region" aria-label="Guided breathing exercise"><h3>Try it now: Box Breathing</h3><p>A simple grounding exercise you can use anytime. Follow the animation at your own pace.</p><div class="breath-box" id="breath-box"><div class="breath-circle" id="breath-circle"></div><p class="breath-instruction" id="breath-instruction"></p></div><button class="btn btn-secondary" id="breath-toggle">Start breathing exercise</button></div>
        <div class="overlay-cards"><a href="#" class="overlay-card overlay-card-link"><h4>Box Breathing</h4><p>A 4-count breathing technique used to slow your heart rate and regain focus.</p><span class="wellness-tag">Beginner</span></a><a href="#" class="overlay-card overlay-card-link"><h4>5 Minute Stress Relief</h4><p>A short guided breathwork session to release tension.</p><span class="wellness-tag">All levels</span></a><a href="#" class="overlay-card overlay-card-link"><h4>4-7-8 Calming Breath</h4><p>Activate your parasympathetic nervous system within minutes.</p><span class="wellness-tag">Beginner</span></a><a href="#" class="overlay-card overlay-card-link"><h4>Grounding Breathwork for Flashbacks</h4><p>A guided practice to bring you back to the present.</p><span class="wellness-tag">All levels</span></a><a href="#" class="overlay-card overlay-card-link"><h4>Morning Reset: 3 Minutes to Start Your Day</h4><p>A short breathwork routine to set a calm intention.</p><span class="wellness-tag">Beginner</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="overlay" id="overlay-yoga" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog" aria-label="Yoga and wellness resources">
